1. API Gateway Pattern
====================================================================
Why?

Single entry point for all clients.

Client
   |
   v
API Gateway
   |
   v
Microservices

====================================================================
Responsibilities:

Authentication
Authorization
Routing
Rate Limiting
Logging
====================================================================

Example:


/api/risks
/api/controls
/api/audit


All requests first reach gateway.
====================================================================
Benefit
Centralized Security
Reduced Client Complexity
Single Endpoint


====================================================================
2. Database Per Service Pattern
====================================================================
Each service owns its database.

Risk Service
      |
   Risk DB

Control Service
      |
  Control DB

Audit Service
      |
  Audit DB

====================================================================


Why?

Avoid tight coupling.

Benefit
Independent Deployment
Independent Scaling
No Shared Schema
====================================================================
3. Event-Driven Architecture
====================================================================


Most important pattern used.



Risk Created
      |
      v
risk-topic
      |
      +---- Compliance Service
      |
      +---- Audit Service
      |
      +---- Notification Service

====================================================================


Producer:

kafkaTemplate.send(
   "risk-topic",
   riskEvent
);

====================================================================



Consumer:

@KafkaListener(topics="risk-topic")
public void consume(RiskEvent event){
   process(event);
}



Benefit
Loose Coupling
Scalability
Asynchronous Processing


====================================================================
4. Saga Pattern
====================================================================


Used when multiple services participate in one business transaction.

Example

Risk Creation Workflow

Step 1 Risk Service
Step 2 Control Service
Step 3 Approval Service
Step 4 Audit Service


====================================================================

Success Flow


Risk Created
      |
Control Created
      |
Approval Created
      |
Audit Entry Created



====================================================================

Failure Flow



If Approval fails:



Approval Failed
      |
Compensating Transaction
      |
Rollback Control
      |
Rollback Risk



====================================================================

Benefit:

No Distributed Transactions
Suitable for Microservices
Eventual Consistency



====================================================================
5. Circuit Breaker Pattern
====================================================================


Used for external API calls.

Risk Service
      |
      v
External System


If target system fails repeatedly:

Closed
 -> Open
 -> Half Open
 -> Closed



====================================================================

Using Resilience4j:

@CircuitBreaker(name="riskService")
public Response getRisk(){
    return client.call();
}


====================================================================


Benefit
Prevents Cascading Failures
Improves Stability





====================================================================
6. Retry Pattern
====================================================================

Temporary failures handled automatically.


@Retry(name="riskApi")
public Response getData(){
    return service.call();
}




Retry Sequence:

Try 1
Try 2
Try 3
Fail




Benefit
Handles Transient Failures
Improves Reliability



====================================================================

7. Dead Letter Topic (DLT)
====================================================================


Failed Kafka messages moved to DLT.

risk-topic
     |
     +---- Success
     |
     +---- risk-dlt


Example:

Invalid JSON
Database Down
Validation Error

Benefit
No Data Loss
Easy Reprocessing


====================================================================
8. Outbox Pattern
====================================================================

Used to avoid DB-Kafka inconsistency.

Without Outbox:

DB Saved
Kafka Publish Failed


Data becomes inconsistent.




====================================================================
With Outbox:

Save Business Data
       |
       v
Save Outbox Event
       |
       v
Publisher Reads Outbox
       |
       v
Kafka Topic


====================================================================

Benefit
Guaranteed Event Delivery
Reliable Messaging




====================================================================
9. CQRS Pattern (Reporting)

====================================================================

In banking systems reports require heavy reads.

Write Service
      |
      v
Kafka
      |
      v
Read Database

Benefit
Fast Reporting
Separate Read/Write Scaling


====================================================================



