1. How Events Flow Through Kafka Streams
====================================================================

Step 1: Producer Publishes Event


kafkaTemplate.send("payment-topic", paymentEvent);


Example:

{
  "paymentId":"P1001",
  "amount":5000,
  "status":"INITIATED"
}


Stored in:

payment-topic


====================================================================


Step 2: Kafka Streams Consumes Event
StreamsBuilder builder = new StreamsBuilder();

KStream<String, PaymentEvent> stream =
      builder.stream("payment-topic");


Kafka Streams continuously polls records from the topic.



payment-topic
     |
     v
Kafka Streams


====================================================================
Step 3: Process Event


Validation
stream.filter(
    (key,value) -> value.getAmount() > 0
);


====================================================================


Transformation
stream.mapValues(event -> {
    event.setStatus("VALIDATED");
    return event;
});



====================================================================


Enrichment
stream.mapValues(this::enrichCustomerInfo);



====================================================================


Step 4: Publish To Output Topic
processedStream.to("validated-payment-topic");



====================================================================


Flow:

payment-topic
      |
Kafka Streams
      |
validated-payment-topic



====================================================================



Step 5: Consumer Reads Processed Data
@KafkaListener(topics="validated-payment-topic")
public void consume(PaymentEvent event){
     saveToDatabase(event);
}



